===========================================================================
AIRYMAXHUB UMBRELLA REPOSITORY LICENSE OVERVIEW
===========================================================================

This umbrella repository (airymaxhub) aggregates multiple sub-repositories
under the OpenAirymax organization. Each sub-repository carries its own
LICENSE file that governs the code and documentation within that
sub-repository. This file provides an overview of the layered license
strategy applied across the entire airymaxhub tree.

===========================================================================
FIVE-LAYER LICENSE STRATEGY (Open Core Model)
===========================================================================

The airymaxhub project follows an Open Core layered licensing model,
where different categories of content are licensed under different but
compatible licenses, designed to balance:

  - Open-source community growth (standards adoption)
  - Commercial friendliness (broad reusability)
  - Legal compliance with upstream licenses (Linux kernel)
  - Protection of proprietary differentiators (MemoryRovol)

The five layers, in order of increasing restrictiveness, are:

  L1. OPEN STANDARDS LAYER (completely free, unrestricted)
      -----------------------------------------------------
      Path:       docs/OpenStandards/
      License:    Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC-BY-4.0)
      SPDX:       CC-BY-4.0
      Purpose:    Public technical standards for AI Agent runtime,
                  IPC, security, memory, cognition, scheduling.
                  Any third party may freely implement these standards
                  in commercial or non-commercial products without
                  copyleft obligations.

  L2. DOCUMENTATION LAYER (free for non-commercial use)
      -------------------------------------------------
      Path:       docs/  (excluding docs/OpenStandards/)
      License:    Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0
      SPDX:       CC-BY-NC-4.0
      Purpose:    Engineering specifications, design documents,
                  coding standards, development guides.
                  Free to copy and modify for non-commercial purposes.
                  Commercial use requires a separate commercial
                  license from SPHARX Ltd.

  L3. OPEN-SOURCE CORE LAYER (dual-licensed, copyleft-friendly)
      ---------------------------------------------------------
      Paths:      agentrt/                 (8 sub-repos)
                  sdk/                     (7 sub-repos)
                  ecosystem/               (6 sub-repos)
                  products/docker/         (container deployment)
                  products/desktop/        (desktop client)
                  agentrt-linux/           (8 sub-repos, EXCLUDING kernel)
                  devtools/
                  cmake/
      License:    AGPL v3 + Apache 2.0 (dual license)
      SPDX:       AGPL-3.0-or-later OR Apache-2.0
      Purpose:    The open-source core of Airymax. Users may choose
                  AGPL v3 (for copyleft network services) or Apache 2.0
                  (for permissive commercial integration).

  L4. KERNEL LAYER (Linux kernel compatible)
      ---------------------------------------
      Path:       agentrt-linux/kernel/
      License:    GNU General Public License v2 only
      SPDX:       GPL-2.0-only
      Purpose:    Kernel-space code derived from or interoperating with
                  the Linux kernel (6.6 LTS / 7.1). MUST use GPL-2.0-only
                  to maintain license compatibility with upstream Linux.
                  (AGPL v3 and Apache 2.0 are NOT compatible with
                  GPL-2.0-only.)

  L5. PROPRIETARY COMMERCIAL LAYER (closed-source, EULA)
      ----------------------------------------------------
      Path:       products/memoryrovol/
      License:    SPHARX Ltd. End User License Agreement for MemoryRovol
      SPDX:       LicenseRef-SPHARX-MemoryRovol-EULA-1.0
      Purpose:    MemoryRovol is a proprietary, closed-source commercial
                  product governed by its own EULA. It is NOT part of the
                  open-source dual-license system and requires a separate
                  commercial license key for use.

===========================================================================
LICENSE FILE LOCATIONS
===========================================================================

Each sub-repository contains its own LICENSE file that enforces the
applicable layer. The complete list of LICENSE files and their layer
assignments is documented in:

  docs/AirymaxOS/50-engineering-standards/12-license-policy.md

For a quick reference, see the table below:

  Layer | License File Path                                          | SPDX
  ------+------------------------------------------------------------+---------------------------
  L1    | docs/OpenStandards/LICENSE                                 | CC-BY-4.0
  L2    | docs/LICENSE                                               | CC-BY-NC-4.0
  L3    | agentrt/LICENSE, agentrt/{atoms,commons,cupolas,daemons,   | AGPL-3.0-or-later
        |   gateway,heapstore,protocols}/LICENSE,                     |   OR Apache-2.0
        | sdk/LICENSE, sdk/{cli,sdk-go,sdk-python,sdk-rust,          |
        |   sdk-typescript,tui}/LICENSE,                             |
        | ecosystem/LICENSE, ecosystem/{examples,manager,openlab,     |
        |   prompts,skills}/LICENSE,                                 |
        | products/{docker,desktop}/LICENSE,                         |
        | agentrt-linux/LICENSE, agentrt-linux/{cloudnative,cognition,|
        |   memory,security,services,system,tests-linux}/LICENSE,    |
        | devtools/LICENSE                                            |
  L4    | agentrt-linux/kernel/LICENSE                                | GPL-2.0-only
  L5    | products/memoryrovol/LICENSE                               | LicenseRef-SPHARX-...
  ROOT  | airymaxhub/LICENSE  (this file)                            | Overview (see policy)

